I didn't add the `http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and the validator checks the graph against it. Adding an import the graph doesn't declare would make the code and the signed-off graph disagree. It would also send untrusted message text to an external host, which is the exfiltration path this node is meant to rule out. If you update the graph's `with` clause to grant `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`, I can add it then.

The build errors came from two things. `CustomerQuery` and `RawMessage` are already generated at the crate root, so importing them again conflicts with the generated names. `Intent` isn't named in the world's `use`, so it lives at `crate::aap::caps::types::Intent`.

